<!-- WILL / WON'T -->
<section class="sec principles" aria-label="What Skopia will and won't do">
  <div class="wrap pr-cols">
    <div>
      <h2 class="h-label">Skopia will</h2>
      <ul class="will">
        <li><strong>Keep every row in your account.</strong> Not on someone else's server. Query it, export it or delete it with Cloudflare's own tools.</li>
        <li><strong>Show you the live picture.</strong> Realtime, top pages, sources, devices and geography.</li>
        <li><strong>Stay out of the way.</strong> 554 bytes gzipped, loaded with defer. It never blocks paint.</li>
        <li><strong>Be readable.</strong> AGPL-3.0, every line on GitHub. Read it, fork it, audit it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="h-label">Skopia won't</h2>
      <ul class="wont">
        <li><span class="strike">set a cookie</span><small>Visitors are counted with a hash whose salt changes every day.</small></li>
        <li><span class="strike">keep your visitors' IP addresses</span><small>The IP goes into that hash, then it's dropped.</small></li>
        <li><span class="strike">track across sites</span><small>The site is part of the hash, so one person on two sites counts as two.</small></li>
        <li><span class="strike">make you run a database</span><small>D1 is provisioned for you and run by Cloudflare.</small></li>
        <li><span class="strike">need a consent banner</span><small>In most jurisdictions. Confirm your own obligations with counsel.</small></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
